WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.860
shortly after Joe Biden won and it looked
like control of the U.S. Senate was going

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:07.680
to come down to two seats in Georgia.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:15.250
We knew that the best case scenario was 50/50,
with Democrats technically having a majority

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:20.280
because Kamala Harris gets to cast the tie,
breaking 51 votes.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:25.960
If all 50 Democrats are on the same page about
a particular issue or bill or whatever the

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:26.960
case may be.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.230
And so when we knew that that was going to
be the scenario, I started talking about Joe

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:39.249
Manchin and as the most conservative Democratic
senator in the U.S. Senate, I said back in

00:00:39.249 --> 00:00:45.379
November, December, Joe Manchin could be a
formidable impediment to Joe Biden getting

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:48.559
things done that he claims that he wants to
do.

00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:50.460
And my audience was split.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.839
Some in my audience understood the magnitude
of it.

00:00:52.839 --> 00:00:55.850
They understood why I was talking about Joe
Manchin.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:01:00.460
Some denied it and said Joe Manchin is not
going to really be that big of an obstacle.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:05.750
As we are clearly seeing now with Joe Manchin
opposed to so much of what Joe Biden wants

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:12.620
to do, we realize that he is indeed a formidable
obstacle.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:18.220
And now on top of this, we're learning something
about why and it's absolutely horrifying.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:24.670
In an interview with CNN over the weekend,
Senator Joe Manchin straight up says the January

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:33.300
6th Trump riots made him realize that we need
bipartisanship and we need to placate the

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:40.351
rioters with what he correctly says in this
clip that I'm going to play for you, that

00:01:40.351 --> 00:01:47.050
he was shocked by the direct attack on the
basic institutions of government and democracy

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:51.030
on January 6th, as we all should have been
and many of us were.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:56.500
But Joe Manchin says it made him decide he
needs to seek bipartisanship, period.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:04.140
He can't just go along with whatever Joe Biden
wants to do, the violence and what is essentially

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.620
the terrorism, the hostage taking.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:11.090
It worked in exactly the way that the terrorists
wanted.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:17.019
He is saying when terrorists hold me hostage,
I negotiate with them, listen to him, and

00:02:17.019 --> 00:02:18.319
then we're going to talk about it more.

00:02:18.319 --> 00:02:23.030
January six changed me and I was very clear
with everybody I never thought in my life,

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:28.579
I never read in history books to where our
form of government had been attacked at our

00:02:28.579 --> 00:02:32.579
seat of government, which is Washington, DC
and our capital by our own people.

00:02:32.579 --> 00:02:35.580
Now, the British did it, but not Americans.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.159
So something told me, wait a minute, pause.

00:02:38.159 --> 00:02:39.189
Hit the pause button.

00:02:39.189 --> 00:02:40.329
Something's wrong.

00:02:40.329 --> 00:02:42.700
You can't have this many people split to where
they want to go to war

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:43.700
with each other.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:49.060
Can you imagine Joe Manchin now stands in
the way of much of what Joe Biden wants to

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.709
do because he wants.

00:02:51.709 --> 00:02:57.360
Bipartisanship, thanks to people who stormed
the Capitol and did violence and committed

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.969
crimes and wanted the loser, Donald Trump,
to be installed as president.

00:03:01.969 --> 00:03:06.380
That's what they wanted, completely anti-democratic,
completely against the law, completely against

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:11.400
everything the country supposedly stands for,
whether Joe Manchin intends to or not, whether

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:15.569
Joe Manchin realizes it or not, he is encouraging
them to do it again.

00:03:15.569 --> 00:03:21.049
The reaction to the violent riots should not
be you know, that really shocked me that they

00:03:21.049 --> 00:03:23.109
were willing to do that.

00:03:23.109 --> 00:03:27.529
So I'm going to be more bipartisan and play
to their side so that we don't have as big

00:03:27.529 --> 00:03:30.150
of a disagreement in this country between
right and left.

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:31.590
That's the wrong reaction.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:37.390
He is playing to those who rioted, saying,
I will now vote in the Senate in a different

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:38.639
way.

00:03:38.639 --> 00:03:43.989
That will be closer to what those who rioted,
what the reaction should be.

00:03:43.989 --> 00:03:46.010
Those who rioted should be held accountable.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:49.219
There should be consequences rather than rewards.

00:03:49.219 --> 00:03:51.579
He's talking about rewarding them.

00:03:51.579 --> 00:03:56.689
We must not give the impression that what
they did on January 6th is valid political

00:03:56.689 --> 00:03:58.169
speech or activism.

00:03:58.169 --> 00:04:03.669
If you do what they did on January 6th, they
should get nothing from Joe Manchin or anybody.

00:04:03.669 --> 00:04:08.540
You should be invalidating voices that use
crime to get their points across.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:12.689
And yet Joe Manchin is saying, you know, the
riders made me realize we're too divided.

00:04:12.689 --> 00:04:16.290
So, you know, I'm not going to go with stuff
Joe Biden wants.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:23.230
If there isn't Republican support, what what
he wants to bridge the gap between the rioters

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:24.350
and the non rioters.

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:26.140
Give me a break, Joe.

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:32.930
The primary take away from January 6th is
that we have to protect the country from the

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:37.320
influence of people who are willing to do
what the rioters did.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:43.550
We should be giving them no role in policy
or governance whatsoever not to cater to them.

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:45.870
This is backwards logic from Joe.

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:46.870
It's not even logic.

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:47.870
Quite right.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:50.190
I don't know what it's there's no logic here.

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:51.740
It changed him.

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:57.030
He says apparently for the worse, they intimidated
him and it worked.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:05:02.220
He should be recommitting to only consider
the ideas of non rioters.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.860
It's a completely bizarre argument and reaction.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:06.880
They were trying to kill him.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:11.720
And his reaction is, let me let me give them
more of what they want after 9/11.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:15.020
Should we have said, you know, we maybe we
should look at giving al-Qaida some stuff?

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:16.120
I don't know.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:19.520
I mean, they were really angry and so they
did 9/11.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.670
Maybe that anger means we should give them
some stuff.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:22.760
It's backwards.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:23.760
It's backwards.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:27.080
So that's Joe Manchin giving us now a framework.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:29.830
We've been wondering, you know, what is it
with Joe Manchin?

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:34.220
This is we now understand the framework under
which Joe Manchin is operating in the Senate.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.760
I don't know how you work with a guy like
that.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:39.510
And, you know, I know that we often have this
debate.

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:43.090
Well, just primary Joe Manchin and like, put
Bernie Sanders in.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:46.340
I don't think Bernie Sanders wins in West
Virginia.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:48.020
I think you just get a Republican.

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:50.280
It's about we have to look at other places.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:53.080
I mean, short primary Manchin if you want
it.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.640
But if you successfully do, it might lead
to a Republican.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:06:01.280
But at the same time, we have to be looking
at states, races in which in twenty twenty

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:06.830
two, a Republican senator can be removed and
a Democratic senator can be put in, hopefully

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:13.040
one who is more reliable vote than Joe Manchin
has been.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:14.100
Let me know what you think.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:17.340
This strikes me as could not possibly be more
backwards.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:18.340
Find me on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:18.479
Let me know your thoughts.

